I stand up slowly and get dressed.
I put on my dark green coat because it is wet and cold outside.
Then I walk slowly to the doctor's practice.
My head hurts.
I arrive at the practice and go straight to the reception.
The receptionist looks at me.
"Good morning," I say quietly.
"I have an appointment at half past ten."
"Good morning, Frau Flores," she says friendly.
"I need your health insurance card, please."
I open my bag and give her the health insurance card.
She takes the card and types something into the computer.
After a short moment, she gives me the card back.
"Thank you very much," she says.
"You should take a seat in the waiting room."
"The doctor will call you then."
I nod silently, because my throat hurts too.
Then I slowly walk into the waiting room.
